        <name>loadDefaultRules</name>
        <qualifiedname>themis::observability::AlertingEngine::loadDefaultRules</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Load Default Rules. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Load predefined alert rules that cover the major error and performance event categories:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>High CPU utilization (&gt; 80%)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>High memory utilization (&gt; 90%)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>P99 query latency spike (&gt; 1000 ms)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Elevated error rate (&gt; 5%)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Low disk free space (&lt; 10%)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Deep query queue (&gt; 100 pending queries)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>High cache miss rate (&gt; 50%)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Storage write amplification (&gt; 20×)</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Existing rules with the same IDs are skipped (idempotent).</para>
<para>Calls: getRule(), has_value(), addRule(), THEMIS_WARN(), error(), message(). </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
